"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2981,"**
Narrated to us Abu 'Ammar Husayn ibn Hurayth, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim, narrated to me al-Awza'i, narrated to me al-Zuhri, narrated to me Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, narrated to me Abu Hurayrah (RA) who said:

The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to us while we were in **Mina**:

*""We shall be staying tomorrow at al-Khayf of Banu Kinanah.""*

Bundar said: *""When they took an oath, it was only at the place where they took an oath upon disbelief. That was when Quraysh and Kinanah made a pact against Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib that they would not marry them nor deal with them until they surrendered the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to them.""* This refers to **al-Muhassab**."
2982,"**
Narrated to us Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la and Muhammad ibn Nasr (may Allah have mercy on them), both said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn Bukayr, narrated to us al-Awza'i, narrated to me Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (RA) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said something similar to the following:

Narrated to us al-Rabi', narrated to us Bishr ibn Bakr, he informed me al-Awza'i, from Ibn Shihab, similarly except that they said: ""Do not marry them, and let there be no dealings between them and you until they send to them the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).""

Al-Rabi' and Yunus said: ""Where they took an oath upon disbelief.""

Bishr said: ""When they swore upon disbelief."""
